   "body": "Adversarial review round 1 (Fable 5.2, read-only sub-agent of cloud/orch), verbatim:\n\n**Adversarial review (Fable 5.2): REQUEST CHANGES** — head 8a8d3164\n\n1. **Medium** — `docs/adr/0013-storage-tiers.md:231`: the row says \"the `icon` an **app-chosen** dated icon replaced\". The app never chooses an icon. `icon_previous` is written only in `AppIconSettingsModel.select` → `rememberPrevious` (`App/SwiftHFR/Settings/AppIconSettingsModel.swift:75-97`), which is the user's tap in the picker. The only other `setAlternateIconName` call is the user's \"Oui\" answer (`AppIconSeasonModel.swift:62`). A reader of the ADR would conclude the app switches icons by itself, which contradicts the rationale of the row just above (\"no icon change under the user\", line 230). Fix: \"the `icon` a dated icon the user picked replaced\". The same wording is in the doc comment at `Packages/HFRKit/Sources/HFRStorage/Settings/SettingKey.swift:71`; fix it there or open an issue.\n2. **Detail, not blocking, outside this diff** — same class of gap: `app_lock_enabled` and `app_lock_grace_seconds` (LOT-173) are in the `SettingScopeTests` matrix, which says it mirrors appendix E \"key by key\", but the ADR has no row for them (0 matches for `app_lock`). This needs its own issue.\n\n**Verified**\n- Key names, `SettingKey` symbols and \"LOT-189, new key\" match `SettingKey.swift:70-76`.\n- Scope is `.device`: neither key is `.synced`, and `SettingScopeTests.swift:29-30` agrees.\n- The `<icon>:<year>` format matches `AppIconSeasonModel.token` (`AppIconSeasonModel.swift:77-80`).\n- \"Once per season, per device\" matches `checkAtLaunch` and `markAsked`.\n- Both rows have the table's 7 columns, in the style of the other new-key rows (`theme_id`, `mp_list_display`), with no tabs.\n- Section 1 rule 4 (device semantics: icon) is respected; the KVS budget is unaffected because the keys are device-only.\n- Diff is 1 file, +2 lines. No tests or lint were run: the change is docs-only, and the scope test was read, not executed.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
