   "body": "Adversarial review round 2 (Fable 5.2, read-only sub-agent of cloud/orch), verbatim:\n\n**Adversarial review (Fable 5.2): APPROVE** — head 7d692097\n\nNo open finding on this PR.\n\n1. **Finding 1 (round 1, Medium): fixed.** `docs/adr/0013-storage-tiers.md:231` now reads \"the `icon` that a dated icon the user picked replaced\". That matches the only writer of `icon_previous`, `AppIconSettingsModel.select` → `rememberPrevious` (`App/SwiftHFR/Settings/AppIconSettingsModel.swift:75-97`), and no longer contradicts the `icon` row's \"no icon change under the user\" (line 230).\n2. **Left out of this PR, to track.** The doc comment at `Packages/HFRKit/Sources/HFRStorage/Settings/SettingKey.swift:71` still says \"app-chosen dated icon\". Leaving it out of a docs-only PR is reasonable, but a PR note is lost at merge: it needs an issue, or a fix in the next PR that touches that file.\n3. **Out of scope, to track (round 1 finding 2).** Appendix E still has no row for `app_lock_enabled` and `app_lock_grace_seconds` (LOT-173), which the `SettingScopeTests` matrix lists. Same need: an issue.\n\n**Verified**\n- `git diff 8a8d3164..HEAD` changes one line, the wording of the `icon_previous` row, and nothing else.\n- The whole PR (`origin/dev-swift...HEAD`) is 1 file, +2 lines, with both rows at the table's 7 columns and no tabs.\n- Key names, `SettingKey` symbols, device scope and the `<icon>:<year>` token were checked against `SettingKey.swift:70-76`, `SettingScopeTests.swift:29-30` and `AppIconSeasonModel.swift:77-80` in round 1 and are unchanged.\n- No tests or lint were run: the change is docs-only.\n\nPoints 2 and 3 are tracked in #863.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
